Phase 2: Install CLI Tools on the Jenkins Host / Agent
Your Jenkins pipeline executes shell commands (sh) expecting CLI tools pre-installed on the host machine running the Jenkins agent:

1. SonarQube Scanner

docker run -d --name sonarqube \
  --hostname sonarqube \
  --network devsecops-net \
  -p 9000:9000 \
  -e SONAR_SEARCH_JAVAADDITIONALOPTS="-Xmx1g -Xms1g" \
  -e SONAR_WEB_JAVAADDITIONALOPTS="-Xmx1g -Xms1g" \
  sonarqube:9.9-community

4. Docker & Kubernetes Permissions
Ensure the jenkins user on your server has permission to execute docker and kubectl commands:

Bash
sudo usermod -aG docker jenkins
# Ensure ~/.kube/config or KUBECONFIG exists for the jenkins user so kubectl commands